This test is about 2MeV Fe irradiation pure iron calculated with the SRIM-like algorithm "Kinchin-Pease ; quick calculation of damage"

The input are given in Config.in. This file is internally decomposed into four temp_ifile.iradina which corresponds to the four files generated by the GUI. See this file for details about the input parameters

The outputs are :
2MeV.ions.total and 2MeV.vac.sum. Each file has four columns, col 1 to 3 are interger index of the cells. In the present calculation only column 1 is relevant. To transform the interger index into nm multiply by 1O, into Angstrom multiply by 100.These factors depend on the size of the cells given in Confing.in/ temp_structfile.iradina
Col4 index the concentrations of ions or vacancies. 
In 2MeV.ions.total, the concentration of ions is expressed in (ions/cm3) per (ions/cm2), i.e. in cm-1.
In 2MeV.vac.sum, the concentration of vacancies is expressed in (vacancies/cm3) per (ions/cm2), i.e. in cm-1.
Additional files *repl* and *int* produced by iradina are meaninless for KP quick calculations. 

Figures (*.png) and corresponding xmgrace graphs are plots of the outputs files (x=column one ; y=column 4). In "raw" figures the files are directly plotted. in rescaled figures, x is rescaled to Angstron (*100), y is rescaled in Angstroms-1 (*1e-8).


